  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Familiar Rack",
    "overview": "Everything is where a Hevy user's hand already goes. The look is borrowed on purpose: Hevy's dark surfaces, its blue, its set table, its page bar. Nothing asks to be noticed. A new screen is right when someone who trained with Hevy for years does not stop to look at it.\n\nThe mood is flat, dense and quiet. Rows are compact, parts are split by hairlines, and there is no decoration. The numbers are the content and the interface gets out of their way. Buttons, rows and fields are plain and compact: bare glyphs, grey fills, small corners, small text, styled no more than it takes to find them and hit them.\n\nIt is not upstream openGym's iOS look: no large titles, no inset rounded cards on every screen, no tinted icon tiles, no Apple system colours. It is not a gamified fitness app either: no gradients, no glow, no badges, no confetti, no hero numbers for show.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "A black page with flat content on it. Cards are the exception, not the frame.",
      "One accent. Blue means \"you can tap this\" or \"this is next\".",
      "Colour appears with state: green when a set is done, yellow for a warm-up or a record, red for failure or a destructive action.",
      "Tabular numbers everywhere, so a column of sets lines up.",
      "One page bar on every screen: a bare chevron, a small centred title, plain actions."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Blue Rule",
        "body": "Blue is the only colour that means \"tap\" or \"next\". A thing that is not tappable and not next is never blue.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Earned Colour Rule",
        "body": "Green, yellow and red show up because something happened: a set was ticked, a record fell, a set failed. They are never used to decorate a resting screen.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Grey Until Touched Rule",
        "body": "A value the app filled in is faint grey and medium weight. It turns white and bold once it is typed or its set is ticked (D2).",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No Large Title Rule",
        "body": "A page names itself in the 17px bar. Nothing on a page is set above 22px except a live readout that is the page's whole point.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Rule",
        "body": "Any number that can change or sit in a column uses tabular figures.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat At Rest Rule",
        "body": "Nothing at rest casts a shadow. A shadow means the thing is in the user's hand.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** put a new screen's title in the one page bar: bare chevron, centred 17px/600, plain actions (D49).",
      "**Do** let lists, tables and feed cards run edge to edge, split by half-pixel hairlines.",
      "**Do** keep blue for what can be tapped and what is next, and let green, yellow and red appear only with state.",
      "**Do** draw with the tokens in `theme.css` (`--bg`, `--surface`, `--surface-2`, `--surface-3`, `--label`, `--label-2`, `--label-3`, `--sep`, `--acc`), scoped under `:root[data-ui=\"hevier\"]`.",
      "**Do** keep every target at 44px by extending it invisibly, not by making the control bigger.",
      "**Do** set every changing number in tabular figures.",
      "**Do** keep the faint grey (`--label-3`) at 4.5:1 on a card."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** bring back upstream's iOS look: large titles, inset rounded cards as a page's frame, tinted icon tiles, filled circles behind header icons, Apple's system colours.",
      "**Don't** add what a gamified fitness app has: gradients, glow, badges, confetti, big numbers for decoration.",
      "**Don't** give anything at rest a shadow.",
      "**Don't** fill a danger button red or tint it; red is its text on fill grey.",
      "**Don't** offer a light theme or an accent choice (D17). The light token block exists only for upstream's timer flash.",
      "**Don't** add a second typeface, or set anything above 22px that is not a live readout.",
      "**Don't** put a border around a card, a chip or a field."
    ]
  }
}